Not just the helper dogs, but any monster in a level created for MBF can have 
it's "friendly" flag set, and it will actively help kill hostile creatures for 
you. An interesting side effect (which appears to be intentional) is that 
arch-viles will transfer their friendliness to creatures they resurrect...

This gives me YANI: Arch-Viles in Nethack. They're able to revive creatures that 
have died in the last 50 turns and that left a corpse. Creatures revived by 
hostile Arch-Viles will always be hostile themselves, those resurrected by tame 
Arch-Viles will always be peaceful. Players polymorphed into Arch-Viles (using 
the special monster ability) will have a chance of reviving creatures as tame, 
otherwise they'll be peaceful. Has an claw attack (stolen from some of the other 
Doom demons, since in that game Arch-Viles don't have a close-range attack) and 
can cast fire spells at you. Represented by "&" and would show up only in 
Gehennom. Other details to be worked out should I ever decide to implement this...

